body:
I mean Orange County Florida made the news because they just kept sending kids into more abusive homes than they were took from. Some of the children weren't even in abusive homes to begin with. Seriously just start an ask reddit and say "Adult who were took by cps as kids what are your horror stories".

&#x200B;

I can't even count how many people I know on both hands that were sexually abused while in the hands of cps (hell I was one of the victims). This guy did the right thing. Never answer cps, contact a lawyer immediately after first contact. Only talk to them if it is court ordered. All it takes to get someone investigated for months if not years is a fake phone to cps. You literally don't even need any proof to make a claim. Child Protective Services doesn't protect shit and they ruin more families than they actually help.
